  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "Number of hydrogen atoms per molecule of a hydrocarbon A having <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>85</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>%</mo></math>&nbsp;carbon is (Given : Molar mass of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>84</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> )",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "12",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Using table of empirical formula for the compound:<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width: 500px;\">\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>Element</td>\t\t\t<td>Percentage</td>\t\t\t<td>Mole</td>\t\t\t<td>ratio</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>C</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>85</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>85</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mn>12</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>15</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>H</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>14</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>14</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t</tbody></table><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Thus, empirical formula is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfenced></math>, empirical molecular mass = 14<br />Thus,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>Molecular</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Mass</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>Empirical</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Mass</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>14</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>84</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> Molecular formula <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>12</mn></msub></math></p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
